tion-local `static const uint8_t` arrays:\n52\t//   g_scf_long[8][23], g_scf_short[8][40], g_scf_mixed[8][40]\n53\t//\n54\t// `sr_idx` can reach 8 here (an invalid sample-rate index of 3 combined with\n55\t// MPEG1 gives 9, minus 1 => 8), so `g_scf_*[sr_idx]` may address one row PAST\n56\t// the end of a table. Rows 0..=7 -- every in-bounds case -- are what matters\n57\t// and they are byte-identical to the C tables below. Row 8 is out of bounds in\n58\t// C, where the pointer simply aliases whatever the linker happened to place\n59\t// next; that is undefined behaviour and is genuinely toolchain-dependent (gcc\n60\t// -O2/-O3 emits the order mixed, short, long, while gcc -O0 and clang emit\n61\t// long, short, mixed with padding), so no single stable C behaviour exists.\n62\t//\n63\t// We store all three tables in one contiguous blob reproducing the layout the\n64\t// optimized/CMake-Release C build emits into `.rodata`, verified byte-for-byte\n65\t// against `objdump -s -j .rodata` of the C shared object:\n66\t//\n67\t//   offset   0..320  g_scf_mixed (8 rows x 40)\n68\t//   offset 320..640  g_scf_short (8 rows x 40)\n69\t//   offset 640..824  g_scf_long  (8 rows x 23)\n70\t//\n71\t// So g_scf_mixed[8] aliases g_scf_short[0] and g_scf_short[8] aliases\n72\t// g_scf_long[0], exactly as in that C build. A zero pad follows so the\n73\t// g_scf_long[8] case stays inside our own allocation rather than being UB in\n74\t// Rust. (Rows written shorter than their declared length are zero-filled,\n75\t// which is what C does.)\n76\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n77\t\n78\tconst OFF_MIXED: usize = 0;\n79\tconst OFF_SHORT: usize = 320;\n80\tconst OFF_LONG: usize = 640;\n81\t\n82\tstatic G_SCF_TABLES: [u8; 888] = [\n83\t    0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x06, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x0a, 0x0a, 0x0a, 0x0c,\n84\t    0x0c, 0x0c, 0x0e, 0x0e, 0x0e, 0x12, 0x12, 0x12, 0x18, 0x18, 0x18, 0x1e, 0x1e, 0x1e, 0x28, 0x28,\n85\t  