{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gbarqwykqjslglzxc276dmppdies5bnjcnyh2w2fk4fnwchx26aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_011wKfTZxwCH5NdMvEZhiNfM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('src/lib.rs').read()\ncstart=s.index('// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Scalefactor band tables.')\ncend=s.index('/// `static uint32_t get_bits')\no0=open('.gen_o0.txt').read()\no2=open('.gen_o2.txt').read()\nnew = '''// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Scalefactor band tables.\n//\n// In C these are three function-local `static const uint8_t` arrays:\n//   g_scf_long[8][23], g_scf_short[8][40], g_scf_mixed[8][40]\n//\n// `sr_idx` can reach 8 (sample-rate bits == 3 together with the MPEG1 bit and\n// the extension bit gives 9, minus 1 => 8), so `g_scf_*[sr_idx]` may address\n// one row PAST the end of a table. In C that pointer simply aliases whatever\n// the linker placed next in `.rodata`, so the observable value depends on the\n// order the C compiler emitted the three arrays in -- which is *optimisation\n// dependent*. Both orders that the reference toolchain produces are supported;\n// each is a single contiguous blob byte-identical to the `.rodata` of the\n// corresponding C shared object (verified against `objdump -s -j .rodata`):\n//\n//   default feature set  == `cmake ..` with no CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE (-O0):\n//       0..184  g_scf_long   184..192 alignment pad\n//     192..512  g_scf_short  512..832 g_scf_mixed\n//     => g_scf_long[8] aliases the pad + g_scf_short[0]\n//        g_scf_short[8] aliases g_scf_mixed[0]\n//        g_scf_mixed[8] runs off the end of .rodata (unreproducible)\n//\n//   feature `c_layout_o2` == `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` (-O2):\n//       0..320  g_scf_mixed  320..640 g_scf_short  640..824 g_scf_long\n//     => g_scf_mixed[8] aliases g_scf_short[0]\n//        g_scf_short[8] aliases g_scf_long[0]\n//        g_scf_long[8] runs off the end of .rodata (unreproducible)\n//\n// In both blobs a trailing zero pad follows so the one genuinely\n// unreproducible case stays inside our own allocation instead of being UB in\n// Rust. (Rows written shorter than their declared length are zero-filled,\n// which is what C does.)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n#[cfg(not(feature = \"c_layout_o2\"))]\nmod scf {\n    pub const OFF_LONG: usize = 0;\n    pub const OFF_SHORT: usize = 192;\n    pub const OFF_MIXED: usize = 512;\n''' + o0 + '''}\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"c_layout_o2\")]\nmod scf {\n    pub const OFF_MIXED: usize = 0;\n    pub const OFF_SHORT: usize = 320;\n    pub const OFF_LONG: usize = 640;\n''' + o2 + '''}\n\nuse scf::{OFF_LONG, OFF_MIXED, OFF_SHORT};\n\n'''\ns = s[:cstart] + new + s[cend:]\ns = s.replace('let tables_base: *const u8 = G_SCF_TABLES.as_ptr();',\n              'let tables_base: *const u8 = scf::TABLES.as_ptr();')\nopen('src/lib.rs','w').write(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('Cargo.toml').read()\ns=s.replace('[dev-dependencies]', '[features]\\ndefault = []\\n# Reproduce the `.rodata` array order that the C compiler emits at -O2\\n# (`cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`) instead of the default -O0 order.\\n# Only observable for the out-of-range `sr_idx == 8` row -- see src/lib.rs.\\nc_layout_o2 = []\\n\\n[dev-dependencies]')\nopen('Cargo.toml','w').write(s)\nPY\nrm -f .gen_o0.txt .gen_o2.txt\ncargo build --offline -q && cargo build --offline -q --features c_layout_o2 && echo \"both feature configs build\" && grep -n 'OFF_\\|mod scf\\|use scf\\|TABLES: \\[u8' src/lib.rs | head","description":"Add layout feature to lib.rs and Cargo.toml"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2381,"cache_read_input_tokens":106291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2381,"ephemeral_1h_input_to