✔ |\n| `run_all.sh` | builds C both ways, diffs `nm -D`, runs the suite for 4 feature combos × 2 profiles |\n\n### Tests (via `libloading`, both `.so`s, never calling Rust directly)\n- `phase_b_configs.rs` — 40 tests, randomized (fixed seed) per row, incl. all 65 536 `hdr[1]`×`hdr[3]` pairs and a 200 000-iteration fuzz row\n- `phase_c_errors.rs` — 20 tests pinning exact sentinels (`-1`/`0`/`main_data_begin`), incl. all 4 raw `block_type` values, all 256 values of each header byte, `i32::MIN`/`i32::MAX` limits, negative `pos`, unaligned phases\n- Comparison covers return value, `bs->pos`, and all 32 struct bytes of 4 granule slots (pre-filled `0xA5` so C's *untouched* fields — `region_count[2]`, `subblock_gain[]` — are verified as untouched), plus the dereferenced `sfbtab` row\n\n### Harness validated by mutation testing\n**27 injected single-token mutations, 27 killed, 0 survivors** (every comparison operator, every `get_bits` bit-width, shift amounts, constants, swapped field writes, `.rodata` offsets, `pos`-advance ordering, granule pointer increment, `part_23_sum` accumulation).\n\nTwo remaining `cargo clippy` style lints (`unneeded late initialization`, missing `# Safety`) are intentional — they preserve the literal structure of the C. No `cargo build` warnings. `c_src/` unmodified apart from its own `build/` directory. No binary target exists in either project, so the stdout-comparison step does not apply.","ttft_ms":2664,"type":"result","duration_ms":1041408,"uuid":"38a2fed6-1701-43fb-9617-9e7e2e041460","ttft_stream_ms":2521,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":2521,"queued_turn_count":0}
